{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-64120",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The value $p(4)$ represents the value of $p(t)$ at $t=4.$ In this context, it represents the value of the boat $4$ years after it was purchased.\n\nSubstituting $t=4$ into the expression for $p(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(4) & =10\\,000\\cdot {(0.9)}^{4} \\\\  & =10\\,000\\cdot (0.656\\,1) \\\\  & =6\\,561.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of the boat after four years is $$6,561.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
